        Blocks(
            Paragraph(Text("This unit works inside the original lattice bc-BRST model. The native neutral zero-energy basis has the vacuum v, the c0 state u, one matter oscillator j(axis), its c0 partner k(axis), and the two ghost states z and w. The state space remains the full algebraic State D; E0 is defined as the intersection of the exact charge-zero submodule with the kernel of M D H 0 + G D 0.")),
            Paragraph(Text("The coordinate construction requires both actual matrix equations H*gramComplex D=1 and gramComplex D*H=1. Those equations are used for the L0 basis diagonalization, native spanning and Q action, full-image restriction, and all-energy homotopy. The differential nilpotence theorem and the absolute/full-neutral quotient equivalences, gradings and dimensions additionally carry D.rank=26. The relative equivalence, grading and dimensions require both inverse equations but no rank-26 premise. Native label enumeration and the direct J0 and B0 actions require neither inverse equation nor rank 26; z_absolute_exact likewise holds for arbitrary H without either inverse or a critical-rank premise.")),
            Paragraph(Text("Under both Gram inverse equations, Q sends u to -2 z and sends v, every j(axis), every k(axis), z and w to zero. The resulting differential is transported from the original Q, not substituted for it. Absolute cohomology quotients all E0 cycles by the pullback of the full original Q range, allowing full State preimages. Relative cohomology independently restricts to RelativeSpace=E0 intersect ker B0, then takes cycles and boundaries of relativeDifferential, the original Q restricted to that space. Relative boundaries use preimages in RelativeSpace, not arbitrary absolute preimages or a quotient by B0 images.")),
